# ============================================================================
# pin_assign.pdc  --  HopWINS_UWBDO_FPGA
# Device: iCE40UP5K-SG48I
#
# Sites 14/15/16/17 (IOB_32a_SPI_SO / IOB_34a_SPI_SCK / IOB_35b_SPI_SS /
# IOB_33b_SPI_SI) are deliberately left unconstrained: they are the dedicated
# configuration pins the MCU drives to load this bitstream in SPI slave mode.
# ============================================================================
# 38.4 MHz clock input from the board clock buffer.
# Site 20 is PCLKT1_0, a dedicated global clock input, which is what lets all
# three I/O output registers share one low-skew clock net.
ldc_set_location -site {20} [get_ports CLK_IN]
# MCU link, used by the design only after configuration completes.
ldc_set_location -site {36} [get_ports FPGA_EN]
# 38.4 MHz forwarded out of the DDR output register.
ldc_set_location -site {21} [get_ports CLK]
# One-shot SYNC pulse, out of a registered output.
ldc_set_location -site {10} [get_ports SYNC]
# 1 Hz PPS, out of a registered output.
ldc_set_location -site {9} [get_ports PPS]
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No IO_TYPE or DRIVE constraints here on purpose.
#
# Drive strength and I/O standard are both part of the output buffer delay, so
# the three timing outputs must share whatever they end up with, and the pad
# report already shows all three identical at the tool default. Pinning them
# would only help if the value differed, and picking an I/O standard needs the
# Bank 1 VCCIO rail confirmed first: this project currently maps to LVCMOS33
# while the earlier bring-up project constrained the same pins to LVCMOS18.
# Settle that before adding IO_TYPE, because guessing it wrong changes both the
# input threshold and the buffer delay.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A bank has one VCCIO rail, so every port in Bank 1 must agree on it. CLK_IN
# lives in Bank 1 too, and leaving it at the LVCMOS33 default while the three
# outputs move to LVCMOS18 is what produced:
#   ERROR <71003014> - In the bank [1], VCCIO for [CLK_IN] is incompatible
#                      with port [SYNC] in the same bank.
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18} [get_ports CLK_IN]

ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 DRIVE=4} [get_ports CLK]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 DRIVE=4} [get_ports PPS]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 DRIVE=4} [get_ports SYNC]

# FPGA_EN is on site 36, which is Bank 0, so it has its own VCCIO and is not
# part of the constraint above.
